    "Stack",
    "Recursion"
  ],
  "description": "<p>Given the <code>head</code> of a singly linked list, return <code>true</code><em> if it is a </em><span class=\"cursor-pointer relative text-dark-blue-s text-sm\" data-keyword=\"palindrome-sequence\"><button aria-controls=\"radix-_r_1m_\" aria-expanded=\"false\" aria-haspopup=\"dialog\" class=\"\" data-state=\"closed\" type=\"button\"><em>palindrome</em></button></span><em> or </em><code>false</code><em> otherwise</em>.</p> <p> </p> <p><strong class=\"example\">Example 1:</strong></p> <img alt=\"\" src=\"https://assets.leetcode.com/uploads/2021/03/03/pal1linked-list.jpg\" style=\"width: 422px; height: 62px;\"/> <pre><strong>Input:</strong> head = [1,2,2,1]\n<strong>Output:</strong> true\n</pre> <p><strong class=\"example\">Example 2:</strong></p> <img alt=\"\" src=\"https://assets.leetcode.com/uploads/2021/03/03/pal2linked-list.jpg\" style=\"width: 182px; height: 62px;\"/> <pre><strong>Input:</strong> head = [1,2]\n<strong>Output:</strong> false\n</pre> <p> </p> <p><strong>Constraints:</strong></p> <ul> <li>The number of nodes in the list is in the range <code>[1, 10<sup>5</sup>]</code>.</li> <li><code>0 &lt;= Node.val &lt;= 9</code></li> </ul> <p> </p> <strong>Follow up:</strong> Could you do it in <code>O(n)</code> time and <code>O(1)</code> space?",
  "hints": [],
